			"Message": "chore(config): Update code formatting and project configuration\n\nUpdated and refined project-wide formatting and configuration files to improve developer experience and ensure consistency across different file types.\n\n**Key changes made:**\n- **Updated Prettier configuration** (`prettier.config.js`): Completely restructured with detailed comments and organized sections. Added explicit parser overrides for various file types (JavaScript, TypeScript, Astro, Svelte, Lua, TOML, Markdown, and JSON). Separated JSON handling into strict mode for `package.json` (using `json-stringify`) and loose mode for other JSON files (using `json` parser that allows comments). Clarified plugin ordering with TailwindCSS as the last plugin. Added comprehensive import ordering rules.\n- **Updated EditorConfig** (`.editorconfig`): Added a commented section for Rust files (`.rs`) that explicitly unsets certain formatting rules, preventing conflicts with `rustfmt` while maintaining basic file structure preferences.\n- **Updated README** (`README.md`): Minor grammatical adjustment in the technical vision section, replacing em-dashes with plain text for cleaner rendering.\n- **Updated VSCode settings** (`.vscode/settings.json`): The file was significantly modified (576 → 1678 bytes), though the specific content changes are not detailed in the diff. This likely includes workspace-specific editor preferences.\n\nThese changes ensure consistent code formatting across the codebase while accommodating the specific needs of different file types and development workflows. The updated Prettier configuration provides clear documentation for all formatting rules, making it easier for team members to understand and maintain the code style.",
			"SHA": "5432e9793ca69b0cc62ebd0cf3603aab9d5f6ea2"
