			"Message": "chore(build): Update Cargo configuration and add Tauri plugins\n\nEnhanced the Rust build configuration for improved development experience and added new Tauri plugin capabilities to the workspace.\n\nIn `.cargo/config.toml`:\n- Added `git-fetch-with-cli = true` under `[net]` for more reliable network operations during dependency fetching.\n- Defined a comprehensive `[profile.dev]` section with incremental compilation enabled (`incremental = true`), debuginfo stripping configured (`strip = \"debuginfo\"`), panic set to abort for cleaner crashes, and optimization level 3 applied to all dependencies via `[profile.dev.package.\"*\"]` for faster development builds.\n- Added target-specific `rustflags` for both Apple architectures (`aarch64-apple-darwin` and `x86_64-apple-darwin`) with `-Zshare-generics=y` flag to potentially reduce binary size through generic sharing.\n\nIn `Cargo.toml`:\n- Added two new Tauri workspace dependencies: `tauri-plugin-localhost` (v2.3.2) for localhost server capabilities and `tauri-plugin-log` (v2.8.0) for enhanced logging functionality.\n- Removed the outdated comment `# Tauri (Mountain)` that was no longer relevant.\n- Updated the `rust-version` field from 1.89.0 to 1.95.0 to align with the latest Rust toolchain requirements and ensure compatibility with newer language features.",
